  "claim_short": "The packet gives an affirmative answer. If Tz=lambda z with unimodular lambda, positivity, power boundedness, irreducibility, and the KB property of L^p imply that e=|z| is a strictly positive fixed vector and that T' has a strictly positive fixed functional. Normalizing the principal ideal of e gives a unital positive map R on L^infinity and a unitary u=z/e satisfying Ru=lambda u.",
